  "problem": "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)=x+4{y}^{2}$ on the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{x}{2}}$ given that the area of the region is $\\frac{9}{4}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{\u222c}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{9}{4})}{\u222c}_{D}x+4{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{x/2}x+4{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[xy+\\frac{4{y}^{3}}{3}]_{y=0}^{y=x/2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{24}]_{x=0}^{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}(\\frac{{3}^{3}}{6}+\\frac{{3}^{4}}{24}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}(\\frac{4\\cdot {3}^{3}+{3}^{4}}{24}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}(\\frac{63}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
